<!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__company">Layered Labs · Founder / Product Builder</div>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Hey Cohen</h1>
    <p class="hero__summary">
      An SMS and communications tool for small, relationship-driven businesses, built first for
      Headliner Music Academy. Hey Cohen reads a business's notes, billing, and attendance to
      surface who's worth reaching out to today, drafts the message, and lets staff decide what
      actually sends. Architected, designed, and built end to end.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__meta">
      <div><b>Role</b>Founder · Design + Code</div>
      <div><b>Process</b>Pen and paper, Figma, VS Code, Supabase, Vercel</div>
      <div><b>Stack</b>Next.js · Supabase · Twilio</div>
      <div><b>Platform</b>First module of Odeon</div>
      <div><b>Status</b>Working demo</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__cta">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://pulse-zeta-ruddy.vercel.app/dashboard">Try the demo</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost-light" href="#">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============ BODY ============ -->
<div class="body">

  <div class="block">
    <h2 class="block__heading">Overview</h2>
    <div class="block__text">
      <p>
        Headliner runs on constant communication with parents and students: schedule changes,
        recital reminders, closures, program updates. Before Hey Cohen, there was no texting at
        all. Everything happened in person, through emails written out individually, or phone
        calls that went straight to voicemail. Sending one message and getting a reply could take
        fifteen minutes, with no way to even confirm it had been received.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hey Cohen reads what the business already knows: session notes, billing cadence,
        communication history, attendance. Every morning it surfaces who's worth reaching out to
        and why: a missed lesson, a renewal coming up, a family that's gone quiet. Staff review
        that list, or describe an audience in their own words, and send.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="block">
    <h2 class="block__heading">What it does</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature__title"><span class="dot"></span>Daily insights</div>
        <p>Each morning, Hey Cohen surfaces risks, milestones, and opportunities worth a staff member's attention, grounded in real attendance, billing, and notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature__title"><span class="dot"></span>Natural language search</div>
        <p>Describe who you want to reach in plain language, like "students who haven't attended in three weeks," and Hey Cohen builds the list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature__title"><span class="dot"></span>AI-drafted, staff-approved</div>
        <p>AI drafts each message from contact and program context. Nothing sends until a staff member reviews and approves it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature__title"><span class="dot"></span>Inbox & campaigns</div>
        <p>Two-way conversations, opt-outs, and delivery tracking in one place, replacing scattered personal texts and missed voicemails.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="block">
    <h2 class="block__heading">Inside the product</h2>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="shot__frame">[Placeholder: Dashboard — insight cards showing risk/milestone/opportunity]</div>
        <div class="shot__caption">Every morning, staff open to this. Risks, milestones, and opportunities, ranked by urgency, grounded in real attendance and billing data.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="shot__frame">[Placeholder: Contacts table with natural language search bar]</div>
        <div class="shot__caption">Natural language search, not filter menus. Describe an audience in plain language and get a recipient list back.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="shot__frame">[Placeholder: Inbox with threaded conversations]</div>
        <div class="shot__caption">Every reply lives in one thread instead of a staff member's personal phone.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="block">
    <h2 class="block__heading">What's next</h2>
    <div class="block__text">
      <p>
        Email support is next, even though SMS came first, somewhat against the original plan.
        It's what the data said: staff and parents responded to a text far more than an email.
        "No one checks email" turned out to be closer to literal fact than complaint.
      </p>
      <p>
        One constraint Hey Cohen doesn't control: getting a business phone number approved
        through 10DLC carrier registration, so messages aren't flagged as spam, is a real
        onboarding hurdle. It sits with the vendor, not the product. That's the honest cost of
        running on real SMS infrastructure instead of a black-box sending service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hey Cohen is the first module of Odeon, a suite of tools built to run the businesses I
        own and designed to stand alone as products in their own right. CharterFlow and BandOS
        are next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="block">
    <h2 class="block__heading">Impact</h2>
    <div class="impact">
      <div class="impact__card">
        <div class="impact__value">14</div>
        <div class="impact__label">Students signed up for a single event within two weeks, replacing manual outreach and in-person asks to parents.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="impact__card">
        <div class="impact__value">12% → 23%</div>
        <div class="impact__label">Post-summer re-enrollment rate, nearly double the historical average.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="impact__context">
      Both numbers come from internal students only. Outbound campaigns to lapsed or
      prospective families haven't launched yet. The market standard for a school this size
      is a bolt-on SMS feature like Opus's, $99 a month, with no intelligent cohort targeting.
      Hey Cohen produced these results with a fraction of its intended reach turned on.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>See it working</h3>
    <p>Hey Cohen is a live, working demo. Click through the dashboard, search contacts in plain language, and see a campaign draft itself.</p>
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://pulse-zeta-ruddy.vercel.app/dashboard">Launch the demo</a>
  </div>

</div>

